# COM: End-to-end check of the coverage pipeline over an AMDGPU test-suite slice:
# COM:   a) baseline:       measure coverage of the existing suite slice (the baseline)
# COM:   b) candidate-test: measure coverage of an external test
# COM:   c) incremental:    report lines the new test covers that the baseline misses
# COM:   d) target-lines:   report which specific lines the baseline leaves uncovered
# COM:
# COM: Cross-check: the gaps incremental reports must match the lines target-lines flags, and a
# COM: baseline-covered line must show up in baseline output but not in incremental/target-lines.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/baseline %t/candidate_tests %t/incremental %t/target_lines
# RUN: %coverage baseline --output-dir %t/baseline --sancov %sancov --llvm-lit %llvm-lit --llc %sancov-llc --opt %sancov-opt --lit-filter CodeGen/AMDGPU/loop -j2
# RUN: %coverage candidate-test --output-dir %t/candidate_tests --llc %sancov-llc --candidate-tests-dir %S/fixtures/coverage-new-tests --n 1
# RUN: %coverage incremental --output-dir %t/incremental --sancov %sancov --baseline-output-dir %t/baseline --candidate-tests-output-dir %t/candidate_tests
# RUN: %coverage target-lines --output-dir %t/target_lines --baseline-output-dir %t/baseline --llvm-repo %llvm-repo --target-lines-csv %S/fixtures/target-lines-sample.csv

# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/run_config.json
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/line_coverage_summary.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/llc_address_line_map.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/incremental/new_coverage.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/target_lines/target_lines_uncovered.csv

# COM: AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp:160 is covered by the test suite slice itself,
# COM: so it must appear in line_coverage_summary.csv as full and must NOT be reported
# COM: as a new gain by incremental in new_coverage.csv.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/baseline/line_coverage_summary.csv --check-prefix=BASELINE_CSV
# BASELINE_CSV: {{.*}}/AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp,160,full,

# COM: These lines are uncovered by the test suite slice (none in line_coverage_summary.csv)
# COM: but covered by the external test — manually confirmed at LLVM rev. 40cd48fd385b.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/baseline/line_coverage_summary.csv --check-prefix=SUMMARY_NONE
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,211,none,
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,588,none,
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,596,none,
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,590,none,
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,680,none,

# COM: These coverage gaps, uncovered by the test suite slice but covered by the external test, have been manually confirmed in LLVM rev. 40cd48fd385b.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/incremental/new_coverage.csv --check-prefix=GAP_CSV
# GAP_CSV-DAG: standalone-empty-kernel.ll,{{.*}}/AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,211,
# GAP_CSV-DAG: standalone-empty-kernel.ll,{{.*}}/AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,588,
# GAP_CSV-DAG: standalone-empty-kernel.ll,{{.*}}/AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,596,
# GAP_CSV-DAG: standalone-empty-kernel.ll,{{.*}}/AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,590,
# GAP_CSV-DAG: standalone-empty-kernel.ll,{{.*}}/AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,680,

# COM: AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp:160 is already covered by the test suite slice, so
# COM: incremental must NOT report it as a new gain.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/incremental/new_coverage.csv --check-prefix=NO_BASELINE_GAIN
# NO_BASELINE_GAIN-NOT: /AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp,160,

# COM: The same coverage gaps reported by incremental (GAP_CSV) must be reported as
# COM: all-points-uncovered by target-lines when fed as target lines.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/target_lines/target_lines_uncovered.csv --check-prefix=TARGET_CSV
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: path,line_no,text,symcov_file,point_addresses
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,211,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,588,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,596,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,590,
# TARGET_CSV-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,680,

# COM: AMDGPUAliasAnalysis.cpp:103 is fully covered (full in line_coverage_summary.csv) but
# COM: present in the sample target CSV, so target-lines must filter it out of the report.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/target_lines/target_lines_uncovered.csv --check-prefix=TARGET_CSV_NOT
# TARGET_CSV_NOT-NOT: /AMDGPUAliasAnalysis.cpp,103,
